Ways the change could fail a criterion (what each rating is measured against):

  context-section-optional-background
    [scope_too_narrow] context-section-optional-background/context-subheading-leaks-to-unclaimed
      Content under a sub-heading inside `## Context` (such as `### Measured`) or after a same-level non-mandate heading is not kept in Context. It falls into `unclaimed` or a non-context section, so it is dropped from background or treated as something else.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 1 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    [missing_case] context-section-optional-background/context-heading-name-match-too-strict
      The Context section is recognised only when the heading text lowercases to exactly 'context'. Variants such as 'Context:' or a heading with inline formatting are not recognised. Their content is treated as unclaimed, or as Task content if the heading sits under Task.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#1
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 126 skipped once the defect was covered
    [not_wired] context-section-optional-background/context-not-wired-through-all-decompose-calls
      The parsed context is passed to the decomposer at only some call sites of `_ask_about`. Any other call path decomposes without the background, or the new parameter is missing there.
      src/acceptance/requirement/obligations.py#3
      src/acceptance/requirement/obligations.py#5
      src/acceptance/requirement/obligations.py#6
      pairs: 1 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    [other] context-section-optional-background/context-block-not-separated-from-requirements
      The context block is not kept apart from the requirement list. It is ordered or merged into the same message as the SUBJECT block, so the decomposer reads background as a listed requirement and may derive obligations from it.
      src/acceptance/request_blocks.py#0
      src/acceptance/requirement/obligations.py#2
      src/acceptance/requirement/obligations.py#4
      pairs: 2 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    [missing_case] context-section-optional-background/files-without-context-change-request
      A task file with no `## Context` section produces a non-empty or altered context block. The request then differs from the previous one, so such files are not handled exactly as before.
