      src/acceptance/requirement/obligations.py#4
      pairs: 2 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered

  parse-records-context-field
    [scope_too_narrow] parse-records-context-field/context-subheading-ends-section
      Content under a sub-heading inside Context (e.g. `### Measured`) is dropped from `context` and falls to `unclaimed`, because the nesting check using `context_level` compares heading levels incorrectly or resets the section too early.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 1 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    [missing_case] parse-records-context-field/context-heading-exact-match-only
      Context is recognised only when the normalised heading text equals exactly `context`. Variants such as `Context:` or a heading with trailing punctuation are not recognised, so their content is not recorded in `context`.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#1
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 126 skipped once the defect was covered

  context-blocks-carry-source-spans
    [other] context-blocks-carry-source-spans/non-paragraph-block-span-wrong
      Non-paragraph, non-list blocks under Context (tables, fenced code or quoted logs, blockquotes) are spanned by `_block_span`. That helper may compute offsets differently from `_span`, for example from the wrong line or without the fence lines. The span would then not map back to the block's real position in the source.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 126 skipped once the defect was covered
    [missing_case] context-blocks-carry-source-spans/context-list-item-spans-misplaced
      List blocks under Context are delegated to `_emit_list`, which was written for the other sections. Nested or multi-paragraph list items may be emitted as one span, or with spans relative to the item rather than the file. A reader would have to check that every emitted Context block carries a correct absolute source span.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 1 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    [missing_case] context-blocks-carry-source-spans/context-subheading-content-dropped
      A deeper heading inside Context hits `continue` and `section` stays 'context', so its blocks are still collected. Context-level tracking keys only on the heading level. A Context heading with an unusual form, or a heading that does not follow the nesting rule, could leave later blocks attributed to the wrong section. Those blocks would then be missing from `context` or recorded as unclaimed instead of carrying a Context span.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#1
      pairs: 1 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered

  context-not-reported-unread
    [not_wired] context-not-reported-unread/unread-source-ignores-context-list
      The unread-source computation (the total-coverage check over the parsed lists) may still union only behavior, constraints, scope_exclusions, completion_expectations and unclaimed. The new `context` list would then be missing from the covered set, and every Context block would be reported as unread even though the parser filled `context`. The diff adds the field but does not touch that computation.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#2
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#3
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 12 put to the model, 118 skipped once the defect was covered
    [scope_too_narrow] context-not-reported-unread/context-container-blocks-not-descended
      Inside Context, only paragraphs and lists are handled specially. Every other node type goes through `_block_span` as one span. Container nodes such as blockquotes are descended into everywhere else, and the unread check works on leaf blocks. A blockquote, or a table or fenced block with nested leaves, may therefore not cover its leaf blocks, which would then show up as unread.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 12 put to the model, 118 skipped once the defect was covered
    [missing_case] context-not-reported-unread/context-heading-match-too-strict
      Context is recognised only when the lowercased heading text is exactly 'context'. Variants such as 'Context:' or 'Background', or a trailing-space or markup variant, are not matched. Their blocks fall to the paragraph branch and land in `unclaimed`, so they are reported as unread.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#1
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 126 skipped once the defect was covered
    [condition_inverted] context-not-reported-unread/nested-heading-inside-context-ends-section
      The nested-heading guard decides whether a sub-heading stays inside Context. If the level comparison or the mandate-name test is wrong, or the heading is reset after a deeper non-mandate heading, a sub-heading such as `### Measured` would switch the section away from Context. The blocks after it would then land in `unclaimed` and be reported as unread.
      src/acceptance/requirement/task_file.py#4
      pairs: 2 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered

